From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: keep the finest tiler levels besides the full-FB one

When the GPU has fewer hierarchy levels than needed to cover the
framebuffer from 16 px up (Mali-G31: two), pan_select_tiler_hierarchy_mask
kept the coarsest levels, so every primitive was binned at least at 512 px
and walked by every 16 px tile of that bin. Keep the level covering the
whole framebuffer and use the remaining ones for the finest bins: small
primitives then cost only the tiles they touch, large ones still go to the
top level. nuubOS Home at 1280x720 on Mali-G31: 22.5 -> 10 ms of fragment
time per frame; the per-draw cost of an 8 px shape dropped from ~0.17 ms.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h	2026-10-09 20:54:59.859213337 +0200
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h	2026-10-09 20:54:59.886052198 +0200
@@ -87,15 +87,16 @@
    uint32_t last_hierarchy_bit = util_last_bit(DIV_ROUND_UP(max_fb_wh, 16));
    uint32_t hierarchy_mask = BITFIELD_MASK(max_levels);
 
-   /* Always enable the level covering the whole FB, and disable the finest
-    * levels if we don't have enough to cover everything.
-    * This is suboptimal for small primitives, since it might force
-    * primitives to be walked multiple times even if they don't cover the
-    * the tile being processed. On the other hand, it's hard to guess
-    * the draw pattern, so it's probably good enough for now.
+   /* Always enable the level covering the whole FB. When there are not
+    * enough levels to cover everything, keep the finest ones for the rest
+    * instead of the coarsest: with only the coarse levels every small
+    * primitive is walked by every tile of a 512 px bin. On Mali-G31 (two
+    * levels) a 720p UI of small shapes spent ~0.17 ms of fragment time per
+    * draw that way (nuubOS: 22.5 -> 10 ms per frame).
     */
    if (last_hierarchy_bit > max_levels)
-      hierarchy_mask <<= last_hierarchy_bit - max_levels;
+      hierarchy_mask = BITFIELD_BIT(last_hierarchy_bit - 1) |
+                       BITFIELD_MASK(max_levels - 1);
 
    return hierarchy_mask;
 }
